        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-20261107-z3b7r3j6r5-yr8z7okdet",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "The transfer from Puerto Natales to El Calafate takes about **4–5 hours**. The road crosses mountainous areas and the Patagonian steppe. Along the way, you may see llamas, hares, foxes and alpacas.\n\nCheck in at your hotel.\n\nEl Calafate sits on the shore of Lake Argentino and is the main base for visits to Los Glaciares National Park and the Perito Moreno Glacier. The park has been on the UNESCO World Heritage List since 1987.\n\nEl Calafate is still a small town, with restaurants, bars and shops. After the drive, you can relax by the lake and get ready for your day at the glacier."
    },
